{
  "id": "2026-09-11-model-document-boundary",
  "scope": "model",
  "kind": "review",
  "date": "2026-09-11",
  "question": "What is the smallest schema-valid document and identity contract that all editors and codecs must preserve?",
  "model": "GPT-6 (Codex; exact variant unavailable)",
  "method": "best-api-review/history-v2",
  "trigger": "User invoked $best-api-review model go after selecting the first ledger question.",
  "requirements": [
    "Preserve one schema-valid immutable JSON document model with primary children, optional object metadata and named-root maps.",
    "Every public assertion over unknown must validate the declared base shape it narrows to; malformed document containers must not silently disappear at load.",
    "Preserve schema-directed fitting/defaults without making assertDocument mutate or repair input.",
    "Keep runtime NodeKey, optional persisted element identity and schema lineage/fingerprint distinct where their current lifetimes and jobs differ.",
    "Keep neutral model law in Plite, Plate product defaults and application migrations in their owners, and exact saved-schema rejection before current-schema fitting.",
    "Assessment and recording only; no product changes, publication or downstream execution."
  ],
  "evidenceReuse": "The July historical record has unknown normalized source provenance and a broader read/update/identity question, so no source evidence was assumed current. Fresh source inspection covers the narrower model question, current Plite construction/assertion/replacement, Plate lowering, raw examples and Markdown consumers. Existing package laws were replayed, and a public-API probe reproduced malformed-container disagreement.",
  "summary": "Pursue one private Plite document-shape validation owner across construction, schema assertion and replacement; retain the JSON tree and separate runtime, persisted and schema identities.",
  "verdict": "pursue",
  "previous": "2026-07-23-api-model",
  "relation": "supersedes",
  "alternatives": [
    "Keep/configure the current model: retain the core tree and identity boundaries, but configuration cannot repair the false assertion contract.",
    "Change the existing owner: selected. Reuse one private Plite base-document validation path before entry-specific fitting or full schema assertion, preserving the public calls.",
    "Add a public validated Document wrapper or parser family: rejected; it adds caller conversion and concepts while the existing assertion and JSON contracts already express the job.",
    "Delete/merge: delete duplicate base-shape admission rules. Reject one universal persisted ID because text/element live keys, optional persistent element IDs and schema fingerprints have distinct lifetimes.",
    "Move validation into Plate or codecs: rejected; raw and other ingress paths remain unsound. Keep product root defaults and migrations in Plate/application owners.",
    "Replace the AST with classes or an ID-indexed public store: rejected for this question; no source-backed current benefit earns the additional representation and runtime machinery."
  ],
  "proofLimits": "46 existing tests passed in five source-first package files. A separate 16-row, four-operation-per-row public-API probe reproduced 12 malformed-container cases in raw and closed-schema editors: assertDocument accepts, construction rejects, direct and persisted replacement accept and discard the malformed field. Valid-document and invalid-node controls behave consistently. No fix, browser/device proof, full static typecheck, packed artifact validation, performance gain or exhaustive model audit is claimed. No new runtime store/index/traversal target is selected; traversal/representation changes would require the owning scale probe.",
  "references": [
    "docs/research/decisions/model-document-boundary.md",
